389 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 390 0 R/Alt(A flow diagram of one control loop in six boxes. Top row, left to right: Measure (control and limit accelerometers; spectra, FRF and coherence estimated by the core); the control law file, in purple (a WebAssembly component run in a sandbox with no files, no network, a clock that does not move, fixed random seeds, a memory cap and a time budget per call, which returns a drive request); and the core's checks on the request (right size, finite, a valid spectral matrix with small negative eigenvalues repaired and large ones refused; a failed call holds the previous drive, and three in a row end the run with a controlled stop). An arrow goes down to a box with a thick orange border, the core protections applied to every law: drive ceiling and drive abort, a cap on change per loop, limit notching, envelope alarm and abort, divergence, kinematic and overload checks; it may reduce a request and never makes it more aggressive. An arrow goes left to Drive out: the core synthesizes the drive time history and plays it on the output channels, and a raw-input watchdog on the loop thread trips the emergency stop whatever the law did. An arrow goes left to Recorded: which law ran, by name, version, SHA-256 of the file and parameter values, and, where the module records it, every call's inputs and outputs, written by a writer thread off the loop thread. A dashed arrow labeled next loop returns from Drive out to Measure.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[1]/Pg 838 0 R>>
endobj
