494 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 495 0 R/Alt(A schematic of the loopback bench. Left, a gray box: a computer running the control service and the shell, with no shaker and no amplifier. A double-headed arrow labeled USB connects it to a blue box, the cDAQ-9178 chassis, which holds two modules: the NI 9263 voltage output module (the drive), with its channel AO0, and the NI 9234 delta-sigma input module (the "response"), with its channel AI0. An orange jumper below the chassis connects AO0 to AI0, labeled as the drive fed back as the measured signal; a dashed orange line from a tee on the jumper runs to a green box at right, the bench multimeter, which digitizes the drive outside Hertzforge to time an abort. A line of italic text above reads that the output sample clock is taken from the chassis' AI sample clock, the proven configuration, and that the same run with the route removed is the negative control.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[4]/Pg 842 0 R>>
endobj
